# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   intended to run in multiple environments. Otherwise, consider the following
#   to exclude version lock files from being included in your package
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in collaboration, if platform-specific dependencies need to be
#   included, check for pipenv lock compatibility.
# Pipfile.lock

# uv
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include uv.lock in version control.
#   This is especially recommended for binary packages to ensure reproducibility.
# uv.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock
#   in version control. This is especially recommended for binary packages
#   that rely on poetry.lock to be consistent.
# poetry.lock
# poetry.toml

# pdm
#   pdm recommends to include pdm.lock in version control, which helps produce
#   reproducible builds. It is however recommended to not include pdm-python
#   in version control.
# pdm.lock
# pdm.toml
.pdm-python
.pdm-build/

# pixi
#   Pixi creates a virtual environment in the .pixi directory, just like
#   the venv module creates one in the .venv directory.
.pixi/*
!.pixi/config.toml

# PEP 582; used by e.g. github.com/David-OConnor/pyflow and github.com/pdm-project/pdm
__pypackages__/

